<div style="margin: 0; padding: 0; background-color: #f8f9fa;">
	<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color: #f8f9fa;">
		<tr>
			<td align="center">
				<!-- Main Container -->
				<table width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color: #ffffff; padding: 30px;">

					<!-- Header -->
					<tr>
						<td align="left" style="padding-bottom: 20px;">
							<a href="{{ BaseUrl }}" target="_blank">
								<img src="{{ BaseUrl }}img/icons/icon_ccims_lg.svg" alt="Main Logo" height="60" style="display: inline-block;"/>
							</a>
							<img src="{{ BaseUrl }}img/icons/VST-ECS.png" alt="Secondary Logo" height="60" style="float: right; display: inline-block;"/>
						</td>
					</tr>

					<!-- Divider -->
					<tr>
						<td style="border-top: 4px solid #D53333; padding-top: 20px;"></td>
					</tr>

					<!-- Message Content -->
					<tr>
						<td style="padding: 30px 20px 10px 20px;">
							<p style="color: #344767; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; margin: 0;">
								Dear Team,
							</p>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td style="padding: 10px 20px 30px 20px; color: #344767; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;">
							<p>We are pleased to announce that our <strong>Customer Carry-In (CCI) QR Scanning</strong> process is now ready for implementation.</p>

							<p>Attached is your <strong>unique QR code</strong>, which must be printed and prominently displayed in your receiving area. It should be easily accessible to customers and presented with your assistance during check-in.</p>

							<p>All CCI customers are <strong>required to scan the QR code using their mobile phone</strong> and provide the following details:</p>
							<ul style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 20px;">
								<li>Name</li>
								<li>Contact number</li>
								<li>Email address</li>
								<li>Address</li>
								<li>Unit serial number</li>
							</ul>

							<p>Once submitted, an acknowledgment with a <strong>case ID</strong> and <strong>tracking link</strong> will automatically be sent to the ASP, VST, and the customer, allowing them to monitor the repair progress in real time. The case ID will also be required when logging part requests in PCS. Compliance with this process is <strong>mandatory</strong> for all ASPs.</p>

							<p>Please note that <strong>no additional system</strong> will be provided to ASPs. You are only required to print and display the QR code and ensure the scanning process is properly completed with the end user.</p>

							<p><strong>This new process aims to:</strong></p>
							<ul style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 20px;">
								<li>Enable <strong>VST ECS team</strong> to actively support ASPs through real-time monitoring of CCI transactions.</li>
								<li>Assist ASPs in efficiently tracking warranty claim status from check-in until the unit’s release.</li>
								<li>Provide customers with direct access to their repair status via the tracking link, reducing follow-ups for ASPs.</li>
								<li>Strengthen coordination between VST ECS and ASP to ensure smoother, faster operations.</li>
							</ul>

							<p>We appreciate your full cooperation in implementing this process.</p>
						</td>
					</tr>

					<!-- Footer -->
					<tr>
						<td>
							<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td align="center" style="font-size: 16px; color: #999999; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; padding-top: 30px;">
							This is an automated message – please do not reply.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>
							<br/>
							<br/>
							<br/>
						</td>
					</tr>

				</table>
			</td>
		</tr>
	</table>
</div>
